[[File:Sabine_Starbird.svg|thumb|The starbird of Sabine Wren]]
{{Quote|It's the mark of the Phoenix Squadron. A creature of flight rising in the flames. A symbol of their commitment to victory.|Grand Admiral Thrawn to Agent [[Alexsandr Kallus|Kallus]]|<ref name="Man">{{Rebels|An Inside Man}}</ref>}}
The '''starbird''', also known as the '''Wren Phoenix crest''', was a stylized depiction of a [[Starbird|legendary bird]] rising up in the air, with its wings spread and its head turned to the right. The [[Mandalorian]] weapons expert and [[graffiti]] [[artist]] [[Sabine Wren]] used that symbol as her personal signature.

==History==
{{Quote|There's a lot of meaning to the symbol. According to some, the starbird can never die&mdash;whenever it seems to be gone, it's actually renewing itself in the heart of a nova.|From Sabine Wren's [[Sabine Wren's journal|personal journal]]|<ref name="sketch">''[[Sabine My Rebel Sketchbook]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Vandalized_Imperial_Propaganda_Poster.jpg|thumb|left|175px|An Imperial propaganda poster vandalized with the starbird]]
The design was based on the [[starbird]] of ancient legend.<ref name="begins">''[[The Rebellion Begins]]''</ref> The legend stated that a starbird could never [[Death|die]] and that if it seemed to be gone, it was renewing itself in the heart of a [[nova]].<ref name="sketch" />

At some point, the symbol was adopted by [[Sabine Wren]], a [[Mandalorian]] warrior who put her own artistic spin on the design,<ref name="Rebels Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars Rebels: The Visual Guide]]''</ref> drawing inspiration from [[Janyor]]'s protest [[painting]]s on [[Bith (planet)|Bith]].<ref name="Idiot's Array">{{Rebels|Idiot's Array (episode)}}</ref> During her [[time]] with the [[Spectres|rebels]] from the [[planet]] [[Lothal]], led by former [[Jedi]] [[padawan]] [[Kanan Jarrus]], she painted the symbol wherever the small band would strike. She also painted it on [[Sabine Wren's armor|her breastplate]]. Eventually, it became her trademark,<ref name="Rebels Visual Guide" /> with the design also coming to be known as the Wren Phoenix crest.<ref name="ROVD">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref>

One such victory occurred on Lothal, when Wren sabotaged one of the planet's key air fields. She used the symbol again when she blew away a good part of the ''[[Lawbringer]]'' during the concurring [[Mission to free Wookiee prisoners|skirmish]].<ref name="Spark">''[[Star Wars Rebels: Spark of Rebellion]]''</ref> Again, on the rebels' [[mission to steal Imperial weapons]], she painted her trademark on crates in a [[hangar]] bay on [[Garel]], killing or distracting the pursuing [[stormtrooper]]s to allow the ''[[Ghost]]'', flown by rebel [[captain]] [[Hera Syndulla]], to escape.<ref name="Droids in Distress">{{Rebels|Droids in Distress}}</ref> Wren's sign, however, was not made using ordinary paint, but, instead, was a concoction of her own making that resulted in an explosion. She utilized her explosive symbol again at the [[Spire (Stygeon Prime)|Spire]] on [[Stygeon Prime]].<ref name="Rise of the Old Masters">{{Rebels|Rise of the Old Masters}}</ref>

She also enjoyed vandalizing [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[propaganda]] posters with the starbird symbol.<ref name="sketch" />

''Starbird'' was also one of many fake identities used by the Spectres to identify the ''Ghost''.<ref name="begins" />

Eventually, the use of Wren's starbird had spread among the members of the larger rebellion. Notably, the rebel [[Starship|ship]] ''[[Evac One]]'' bore that symbol on its hull.<ref name="VA">{{RebelsMagCite|17|Vulnerable Areas}}</ref>

[[File:FarnsMonsbeePhoenixCrest-ROUVG.svg|thumb|right|200px|Modified variant on Farns Monsbee's helmet]]
The [[Lothal resistance group]] used the starbird symbol to mark escape routes through the sewers of multiple towns and cities, including [[Jhothal]], which was used by the Spectres on their [[Theft of the TIE Defender Elite|mission]] to Lothal in [[1 BBY]]. Ezra, recognizing the symbol, deduced that it had to have been left by the Lothalian rebels as Sabine would not have had the opportunity to leave her signature there.<ref name="The Occupation">{{Rebels|The Occupation}}</ref> Later, the starbirds in the [[Capital City|Lothal City]] sewers were used by [[C1-10P|Chopper]] and [[Mart Mattin]] to escape after the failed [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel]] [[attack on Lothal]]'s [[Imperial Armory Complex]].<ref name="Rebel Assault">{{Rebels|Rebel Assault}}</ref>

Eventually, Wren's starbird was combined with the [[Saw's symbol|three-pronged symbol]] used by [[Saw Gerrera]] to create the [[Rebel Alliance starbird]].<ref name="AB Update">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref>

Around the time of the [[Battle of Scarif]], the [[Rebel pilot]] [[Farns Monsbee]] had a modified version of Wren's Phoenix crest on his [[flight helmet]].<ref name="ROVD" />

Late in the [[Cold War]], [[Torra Doza]] had a poster with the full starbird symbol on the wall of [[Torra's Quarters|her bedroom]] on the ''[[Colossus]]''.<ref name="The High Tower">{{Resistance|The High Tower}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|I'm probably most proud of the ''Rebels''{{'}} phoenix logo. I made it one day on a whim while working on really early versions of the ''Ghost'' ship, and it's remained unchanged all the way through marketing. It's meant to hint at the Rebel Alliance symbol that will appear in the later films.|Chris Glenn, ''Star Wars Insider'' 154|<ref name="Insider 154">{{InsiderCite|154|Designing Star Wars Rebels|Designing ''Star Wars Rebels''}}</ref>}}
The ''Star Wars Rebels'' phoenix logo was designed by [[Lucasfilm]] concept artist [[Chris Glenn]].<ref name="Insider 154" />

